# zig-f: f folds Zig (#1355). On an if's first line f folds it to its closing brace and f there
# unfolds it; on a line inside a function f folds the function. The file is written here, not in
# the project, which every other scenario counts the files of.
merl
wait Open a file (fuzzy)
run mkdir -p src && printf 'const std = @import("std");\n\npub fn clamp(n: u32) u32 {\n    if (n > 10) {\n        return 10;\n    }\n    return n;\n}\n' > src/clamp.zig
key q
wait merl exited: 0
merl src/clamp.zig
wait A clamp.zig
key :
type 4
key Enter f
wait 1 line
key f :
type 7
key Enter f
wait src/clamp.zig  3:1
key q
wait merl exited: 0
